Drop an FEC shard when its message's buffer can't be allocated.

IHS_SessionFECAdd copied each shard into a calloc() of up to 255 shards of 2048 bytes without
checking it. On a TV the module's memory is fixed (128 MB), and if that allocation failed the
copy would write near address 0, where WebAssembly keeps static data, without crashing there.
The group now stays inactive and the shard is dropped, as a late one would be; a later shard of
the same message tries again.

diff --git a/src/session/fec.c b/src/session/fec.c
index bc831c8..a544c10 100644
--- a/src/session/fec.c
+++ b/src/session/fec.c
@@ -144,6 +144,10 @@ bool IHS_SessionFECAdd(IHS_SessionFEC *fec, const IHS_SessionPacket *shard, IHS_
         group->dataShards = (uint16_t) dataShards;
         group->parityShards = parityShards;
         group->shards = calloc(dataShards + parityShards, shardSize);
+        if (group->shards == NULL) {
+            memset(group, 0, sizeof(FECGroup));
+            return false;
+        }
     } else if (group->packetId != id || group->length != length || group->shardSize != shardSize ||
                group->parityShards != parityShards) {
         return false;
